<FBType Name="I_GetAttribute" Comment="Command GetAttribute( Part 6 - F.58 )">
	<Identification Standard="ISO 11783-6" Description="Copyright (c) 2022 HR Agrartechnik GmbH  &#10; &#10;This program and the accompanying materials are made  &#10;available under the terms of the Eclipse Public License 2.0  &#10;which is available at https://www.eclipse.org/legal/epl-2.0/  &#10; &#10;SPDX-License-Identifier: EPL-2.0  &#10;   &#10;   &#10;see Description Tab">
	</Identification>
	<VersionInfo Organization="HR Agrartechnik GmbH" Version="1.0" Author="Franz Höpfinger" Date="2022-07-08">
	</VersionInfo>
	<CompilerInfo packageName="isobus::UT::I">
		<Import declaration="isobus::UT::Q::const::IDs::ID_NULL"/>
	</CompilerInfo>
	<InterfaceList>
		<EventInputs>
			<Event Name="INIT" Type="EInit" Comment="Service Initialization">
				<With Var="u16ObjId"/>
				<With Var="u8AID"/>
			</Event>
			<Event Name="REQ" Type="Event" Comment="Service Request">
			</Event>
		</EventInputs>
		<EventOutputs>
			<Event Name="INITO" Type="EInit" Comment="Initialization Confirm">
			</Event>
			<Event Name="CNF" Type="Event" Comment="Confirmation of Requested Service">
				<With Var="STATUS"/>
				<With Var="s16result"/>
			</Event>
		</EventOutputs>
		<InputVars>
			<VarDeclaration Name="u16ObjId" Type="UINT" Comment="Object ID" InitialValue="ID_NULL"/>
			<VarDeclaration Name="u8AID" Type="USINT" Comment="Attribute ID of the object "/>
		</InputVars>
		<OutputVars>
			<VarDeclaration Name="STATUS" Type="STRING" Comment="Service Status"/>
			<VarDeclaration Name="s16result" Type="INT" Comment="retval see description"/>
		</OutputVars>
	</InterfaceList>
	<Attribute Name="Documentation" Type="CDATA"><![CDATA[<h1>Command GetAttribute( Part 6 - F.58 )</h1>

<p>This message is available in VT Version 4 and later. This command is used by a Working Set to query the VT for the current state of objects within the VT.</p>

<h2>Valid values for u16ObjId</h2>

<p>The Get Attribute Value command (F.58) is a fixed 8-byte message (Object ID in bytes 2,3, Attribute ID in Byte 4; no Transport Protocol). INIT validates both the object type (iso_has_readable_attribute_id - does this object type have any AID at all, read-only or writable?) and the specific Attribute ID against that type's attribute table (iso_is_readable_attribute), before the command is ever sent - unlike Change Attribute, both read-only and writable AIDs are accepted here. The underlying C implementation itself (cmd_get_attribute_value) performs no type check of its own, only ID_NULL handling; the VT additionally validates the Object ID and the Attribute ID on its side and returns an error response if either is invalid.</p>

<p>ID_NULL (65535) is not a command target but can be used in INIT to deactivate the FB.</p>

<h2>param[in] {objectID, uint16_t}</h2>

<p>Object ID</p>

<h2>param[in] {attributeID, uint8_t}</h2>

<p>Attribute ID of the object</p>

<h2>Return Values:&nbsp;</h2>

<h3>int16_t</h3>

<ul>
	<li><span style="color:#2980b9">VT_E_NO_ERR (0)</span>&nbsp;- OK</li>
	<li><span style="color:#e74c3c">VT_E_DEACTIVATED (-40)</span> - FB deactivated via ID_NULL on INIT</li>
	<li><span style="color:#e74c3c">VT_E_INVALID_OBJECT_ID (-132)</span> - Object ID's type has no readable AID at all (iso_has_readable_attribute_id)</li>
	<li><span style="color:#e74c3c">VT_E_INVALID_ATTRIBUTE_ID (-133)</span> - Attribute ID is not a valid/readable AID for this object type (iso_is_readable_attribute)</li>
	<li><span style="color:#e74c3c">VT_E_NOT_READY (-131)</span> - Buffered: INIT not yet completed / VT not yet ready</li>
	<li><span style="color:#2980b9">VT_E_OVERFLOW (-6)</span>&nbsp;- buffer overflow</li>
	<li><span style="color:#2980b9">VT_E_NOACT (-8)</span> - Command not possible in current state</li>
	<li><span style="color:#2980b9">VT_E_NO_INSTANCE (-21)</span>&nbsp;- No VT client available</li>
	<li><span style="color:#e74c3c">VT_E_HANDLE_INVALID (-128)</span> - ErrorCause: invalid Handle</li>
	<li><span style="color:#2980b9">VT_E_ISO_INSTANCE_INVALID (-129)</span> - Identifier for instance (connection) invalid</li>
	<li><span style="color:#2980b9">VT_E_NOT_ALIVE (-130)</span> - Identifier for instance valid, but VT Dead.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Instanz-Eindeutigkeit (Instance Uniqueness)</h2>

<p>Dieser Baustein erfordert Instanz-Eindeutigkeit bezüglich des Paares (<strong>u16ObjId</strong>, <strong>u8AID</strong>). Es darf im gesamten Programm nur eine Instanz von <code>I_GetAttribute</code> für dasselbe Objekt-Attribut-Paar existieren. <code>u8AID</code> wird bei <code>INIT</code> eingelesen — eine zweite Instanz auf dieselbe Objekt-ID und Attribut-ID wird bei <code>INIT</code> deaktiviert.</p>
]]></Attribute>
	<Attribute Name="eclipse4diac::core::TypeHash" Value="''"/>
</FBType>
